LESSON 16: THE TWO MODES

SW-APL HAS TWO MODES, AND )DIALECT SAYS WHICH YOU ARE IN.
(A) '70 IS MODELLED ON APL\360 OF 1970, USED FROM A 2741
TYPEWRITER TERMINAL; (B) '75 ON THE APL OF THE IBM 5100,
A DESKTOP COMPUTER OF 1975. THE LANGUAGE IS THE SAME CORE,
AND EVERYTHING IN THIS COURSE SO FAR RUNS IN BOTH. EACH
HAS A LITTLE THE OTHER HAS NOT. TRY:

      )DIALECT
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      GO
(A) ASKS THE SYSTEM WITH I-BEAMS: ⌶ AND A NUMBER. ⌶25 IS
THE DATE, ⌶20 THE TIME OF DAY IN SIXTIETHS OF A SECOND, ⌶22
THE ROOM LEFT IN THE WORKSPACE. ITS SETTINGS ARE COMMANDS:
)ORIGIN, )DIGITS AND )WIDTH, EACH ANSWERING WAS AND THE OLD
VALUE. AND )GROUP GATHERS NAMES UNDER A NAME. IN (A) TRY:

      ⌶25
      )DIGITS 5
      2÷3
      )DIGITS 10

IN (B) THESE ARE ERRORS.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      GO
(B) HAS EXECUTE AND FORMAT. ⍎ RUNS CHARACTERS AS APL, AND ⍕
TURNS A VALUE INTO CHARACTERS, SO THAT TEXT AND NUMBERS CAN
BE JOINED. ITS SETTINGS ARE VARIABLES WITH A QUAD IN THEIR
NAMES: ⎕IO, ⎕PP AND ⎕PW, ASSIGNED LIKE ANY OTHER; ⎕TS IS
THE TIME STAMP, WHICH THE 5100 KEPT AS 1900, HAVING NO
CLOCK. IN (B) TRY:

      ⍎'2+2'
      'X=',⍕5
      ⎕PP←5
      2÷3
      ⎕PP←10
      ⎕TS

IN (A) THESE ARE ERRORS: ⍎ IS NOT A CHARACTER THERE, AND A
QUAD IS ONLY EVER INPUT AND OUTPUT.
(TRY IT. TYPE GO TO GO ON, OR STOP TO LEAVE.)
⎕:
      GO
THAT IS THE COURSE. WHERE NEXT:

   )LIB 2      THE COMPANIONS OF THIS COURSE, AS THEY ARRIVE:
               DRILL, EXERCISES MADE AT RANDOM AND MARKED;
               STATS, STATISTICS; AND MORE MATHEMATICS.
   )LIB 1      WHAT SW-APL SHIPS, EACH WITH A DESCRIBE.
   )HELP       THE SYSTEM COMMANDS, AND SW-APL'S DOCUMENTS
               FOR THE REST OF THE LANGUAGE.

CONTENTS LISTS THE LESSONS, TO READ ANY OF THEM AGAIN.

END OF LESSON 16, AND OF THE COURSE. TYPE QUIZ 16 TO CHECK.
